course: dictionary
lesson: 12826
title: Emphasise
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To emphasise something means to make it stand out, so people notice how important it is. «Remember to bring your coat, because it will be cold.» The writer wants you to remember the coat, so the coat is emphasised.
explain: In writing, you can emphasise a point with bold letters, underlining or words like «especially». When you speak, you emphasise a word by saying it more strongly, so the listener hears it. «I did NOT take your pencil» stresses NOT.
explain: Artists can emphasise too. A bright red door on a grey street draws your eye straight to it. To find what is being emphasised, look for what stands out most, and ask why the writer or artist wants you to notice it.
fact: Emphasise is a verb: emphasise, emphasises, emphasised, emphasising.
fact: «Emphasise» means to show that something is especially important.
fact: «Emphasise» can also mean to say a word or sound more strongly.
fact: «Emphasise» can mean to make something more noticeable, like a line or a colour in a picture.
fact: Useful phrases: «emphasise the point» and «emphasise the importance of».
exercise: «The teacher wanted to emphasise the importance of washing hands.» What does emphasise mean here? | *Show that something is especially important | Forget about it completely | Hide it from the class | Say it very quietly
exercise: «She emphasised the word never, so we knew she meant it.» What does emphasised mean here? | Spelled it wrongly | Wrote it in pencil | *Said it more strongly | Said it in a whisper
exercise: Which of these is a way to emphasise a key point in writing? | Leaving it out | Using a tiny font so it hides | Writing it in the corner of the page | *Bold letters
test: The artist used bright yellow to emphasise the sun in her painting. What does emphasise mean? | *Make it stand out more | Make it disappear | Draw it smaller than everything else | Paint it in black
test: Which word would you emphasise when you say «I did NOT take the last biscuit»? | biscuit | I | did | *NOT
exam: Ella wrote «Always check your work» in capital letters and underlined it to emphasise the warning. What does emphasise mean? | To make the warning shorter | *To make the warning stand out as especially important | To write the warning in another language | To hide the warning from readers
